  "id": "dystrophin",
  "term": "dystrophin",
  "definition": "Dystrophin is a protein made by the DMD gene that is found mainly in muscle, but also in the retina and brain. In psychology-related research, loss of the brain form of dystrophin has been linked with cognitive and behavioral changes, including altered responses to stress and problems in synapse development and organization.",
